Aerie-Purpose: Make the vertical strip's state controller keep the sidebar's width in aerie.sidebar.width, never collapse, and not expand on hover, and set the strip's width limits to 260 default and 200 minimum.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/tabs (vertical_tab_strip_state.h, vertical_tab_strip_state_controller_impl.*, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #177. While the layout is the sidebar, the controller reads and writes the width through
aerie.sidebar.width (clamped to 200..400) instead of what a window restored from its session, is
never collapsed (the sidebar hides, it does not shrink to a strip of icons), and reports no expand
on hover. The default and minimum width constants of Helium's strip change to 260 and 200. They are
global to the strip code, so issue #186 (horizontal tabs, which keeps Helium's strip for no layout)
has to look at them again.

